{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-18T18:19:41.055Z","data":{"text":"Done. Summary of what I implemented and verified:\n\n**Implementation**\n- `src/model/requirement_rows.rs` — maps each snapshot's deltas to `requirements` rows: added, then modified, then removed names, then renames keyed on the new name with `renamed_from`.\n- `src/model/task_outcome_rows.rs` — maps every `task_outcomes` column: dominant capability via `owner_capabilities` (max count, first name by bytes on a tie), scope globs/files, the hand-written `verify_kind` (JS `\\s`, one-each quote strip, `.spec.`/`.test.` base-name check, `*` counts 2), `tests_modify`, `verify_starts`, `shares_scope`, position, attempts, first attempt, last dead reason, files touched.\n- `src/model/insert_specs.rs` — `insert_requirements` and public `write_task_outcomes`.\n- `src/model/mod.rs` — 16-table schema, requirement insertion, and `build_read_model` reading `openspec/specs` ownership and filling `task_outcomes` last.\n- `src/lib.rs` — re-exports `write_task_outcomes`.\n\n**Tests**\n- `tests/read_model_specs.rs` — builds the spec-tables fixture, asserts 16 tables, and compares both tables row-by-row with the 6+6 committed JSON rows.\n- `tests/read_model_specs_cases.rs` plus `tests/fixtures/spec-tables-cases/` — reads fixture change folders, calls `write_task_outcomes` with an ownership list built in the test, and covers quotes-only tokens, trailing `/`, `.spec.` names, unowned paths, plus two mutant-killing extras.\n\n**Verification**\n- `cargo test -p osq-kernel-storage --test read_model_specs` passes.\n- `sh scripts/verify-rust.sh` exits 0 (fmt, clippy `-D warnings`, all tests incl. corpus).\n- cargo-mutants over the new source files, `mod.rs` and `lib.rs`: 66 mutants, none missed.\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/216-rust-storage-spec-tables/.run/results/3.md`."}}
